    ---
    
    # THE ACCORD OF STILL POOLS AND FROST ZENITH
    
    ### Being a Treaty of Mutual Obligation Between the Aureate (Merchant Guilds-born) and the ☽'shadow Covens' Order, Concerning Fire-Core Provision, Territorial Administration, and Sanctification Duties Upon the Body of Aurora Berg, Under Amended Stillness-Bound Protocols, Ratified in the Third Season Following the Desecration, Signed at the Waystation Formerly Designated The Frost Zenith
    
    ---
    
    ## PREAMBLE
    
    WHEREAS three seasons have passed since the shallows died and the fish ceased returning; WHEREAS orca raiders now penetrate corridors formerly secured by fire-keeper patrols the ☽'shadow Covens' Order can no longer staff; WHEREAS corruption bleeds outward from The Glow-Fissure into The Still Pools and the lower spires of The Frost Zenith at rates The Communion (elt-sworn) once contained and no longer will; WHEREAS the Flipper Accord, whose language this instrument borrows and whose promises this instrument cannot repeat, has proven insufficient to the changed conditions of a Berg that moves beneath us; WHEREAS the original Stillness-Bound charter, as authenticated by Bursar Ingnao shi'Beacon during the Clever Ice Age, provides insufficient framework for current exigencies—
    
    The parties convene. Not in triumph. In necessity, signed in fire-core light because the aurora wouldn't hold.
    
    ---
    
    ## ARTICLES
    
    **I.** The Aureate (Merchant Guilds-born) shall retain administrative governance of The Frost Zenith, including ration allocation, refugee intake, and memorial designation. The ☽'shadow Covens' Order recognizes this governance without endorsement. Aureate shall submit quarterly fire-core expenditure tallies, auditable under Stillness-Bound protocols, to shadow-parliament observers. The memorial wall in the eastern alcove shall remain unregulated. Someone always carves.
    
    **II.** The ☽'shadow Covens' Order shall guarantee fire-core supply to The Frost Zenith at a rate no less than eleven crystal-weights per unit—the price before the Calving, the price before the dying; any increase subject to joint review. Cores certified under crystalline seal must burn no fewer than forty days. Cores that burn short shall be replaced within three days per Stillness-Bound warranty, a provision hereby restored from lapse and witnessed. The fourteen fire-keepers lost at Terrace Momiou are not forgotten in this numbering.
    
    **III.** Deep-tunnel access below the seventh vein of Nightfall Shelf is restricted to Covens-authorized personnel. No party to this accord shall descend below the sealed gallery. No party shall authorize others to descend. ~~Access restrictions extend to all former Communion initiates without exception.~~ *(Amended: access restrictions extend to former Communion initiates holding knowledge of ☽'glacial Crystalline~ Spiral obtained prior to the schism, excepting adjudicated cases filed under addendum; see* the clause no one reads aloud, *appended.)*
    
    **IV.** Sanctification of corrupted ice within The Still Pools and The Frost Zenith shall be conducted jointly, costs borne in proportion to territorial claim: sixty parts Aureate, forty parts Covens. Re-sanctification following deliberate breach by elt-sworn or unaligned parties shall be borne entirely by the faction governing the breached site. Neither party shall name The Communion directly in enforcement proceedings. Both parties understand why.
    
    **V.** In partial accommodation of principles advanced under The Way∴ens ideology, fire-core extraction techniques for veins above the fifth depth shall be documented and made available to Courier Corps-certified training schools within two calendar seasons. Techniques for veins below the fifth depth remain classified under Mandatum∴absconditu. The ☽'shadow Covens' Order reserves the right to reclassify any technique whose disclosure would compromise deep-vein stability; Aureate reserves the right to audit such reclassification. Both rights are absolute. Both rights contradict.
    
    **VI.** Weal' Clique~ is recognized as co-steward of The Glow-Fissure under existing rotation with ☽'ofund' Guild. Corruption-monitoring data from the Fissure shall be shared with both signatories. The Office of Deep-Archive Provenance shall file reports. Recommendations are not required. What the ice remembers; what the ledger forgets.
    
    ---
    
    ## ENFORCEMENT & DURATION
    
    This accord shall endure for six seasons, renewable by mutual ratification. Violations shall be adjudicated by the Courier Corps under Stillness-Bound precedent—amended, layered, partially illegible, but standing. Territorial disputes unresolvable by review shall be referred to the Shadow Parliament. Fire-core supply interruptions exceeding nine days constitute breach. The seventeen skeletons at Midway Shelf constitute precedent enough for courier inviolability; this accord adds nothing the bones have not already said.
    
    ---
    
    ## SIGNATURES
    
    Ratified at The Frost Zenith, in the converted crystal-vault, by fire-core light.
    
    **Muheiching ai'Frost**, Interim Ledger-Warden, on behalf of the Aureate (Merchant Guilds-born)
    *"Subject to Guild Council review. Pending crystalline audit."*
    
    **Factor Umbrae ☽'Noctlisesecum**, Shadow-Parliament Delegate, on behalf of the ☽'shadow Covens' Order
    
    *Witnessed by:* ☽'Iarlocias the Silent, unaffiliated, who did not sign but whose presence is recorded, and whose testimony regarding deep-tunnel conditions informed Articles III and IV, and who left before the ink set.
    
    ---
